1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:03,373
A tuition email asks you
to pay a new account.

2
00:00:03,723 --> 00:00:06,454
Would you pay it? CEKBAO
checks before you do.

3
00:00:06,804 --> 00:00:08,612
The name is the university's.

4
00:00:08,612 --> 00:00:10,687
The account belongs to someone else.

5
00:00:11,037 --> 00:00:17,138
Singapore police reported at least 20
school impersonation scams since March 2026.

6
00:00:17,488 --> 00:00:21,477
CEKBAO checks it against the
institution's own policy for that date.

7
00:00:25,483 --> 00:00:29,025
This is the real app. We
paste the email into CEKBAO.

8
00:00:29,517 --> 00:00:32,354
It asks us to pay a new
payee and a new account.

9
00:00:34,417 --> 00:00:36,913
We choose the university from the registry.

10
00:00:37,850 --> 00:00:40,608
The date matters, because policies change.

11
00:00:40,608 --> 00:00:42,778
We plan to pay on 15 November.

12
00:00:43,283 --> 00:00:46,163
The check is saved first,
then a worker compares it.

13
00:00:46,650 --> 00:00:49,295
The result: conflicts
with the checked policy.

14
00:00:50,083 --> 00:00:54,158
Next step: do not pay these
details. Contact the university.

15
00:00:54,650 --> 00:00:58,959
Payee, account and bank code
conflict. Currency and method agree.

16
00:01:00,083 --> 00:01:04,990
This is the policy sentence behind the
result, with its version and effective date.

17
00:01:06,017 --> 00:01:08,300
In this preview, fixed rules read it.

18
00:01:08,300 --> 00:01:10,369
The NVIDIA model was not called.

19
00:01:12,883 --> 00:01:17,373
Now, dates. This old invoice
was paid once on 14 August.

20
00:01:17,373 --> 00:01:20,713
The next payment is due on 30 November.

21
00:01:21,950 --> 00:01:26,366
For 30 November, the result is:
conflicts with the checked policy.

22
00:01:26,850 --> 00:01:32,866
Policy version 2026.1 took effect
on 1 September, with a new account.

23
00:01:37,717 --> 00:01:41,386
The August payment matched version 2025.1.

24
00:01:43,700 --> 00:01:46,973
Until 31 August, the old policy applied.

25
00:01:46,973 --> 00:01:50,889
From 1 September, a new
version has a new account.

26
00:01:51,239 --> 00:01:55,933
One invoice, two answers. A match in
the past does not approve a new payment.

27
00:01:59,350 --> 00:02:03,425
Third, a deposit request for a
synthetic Canadian institute.

28
00:02:03,917 --> 00:02:06,541
The result: not enough evidence to verify.

29
00:02:07,450 --> 00:02:10,229
The account matches an
agent's page, but that

30
00:02:10,229 --> 00:02:13,146
publisher has no authority
for this institution.

31
00:02:13,650 --> 00:02:15,865
The French original stays visible.

32
00:02:15,865 --> 00:02:18,258
The translation is labeled unofficial.

33
00:02:19,200 --> 00:02:24,725
The worker is built to call NVIDIA
Nemotron 3 Nano on Nebius Token Factory.

34
00:02:25,075 --> 00:02:27,247
In this preview it was not called.

35
00:02:27,247 --> 00:02:30,025
Code checks every quote,
and fixed rules decide.

36
00:02:31,900 --> 00:02:37,468
231 automated tests pass, and axe
found no accessibility violations.

37
00:02:37,818 --> 00:02:43,130
Limits: synthetic data, no user testing
yet, and no model call in this preview.
